# Every text file in this repo is LF, on every platform, including a
# Windows checkout.
#
# Git's `core.autocrlf` is on by default on Windows, which would rewrite
# line endings at checkout time. That breaks three things here at once:
# the `expected.txt` recordings in `bootstrap/*_corpus/` are compared
# byte for byte; the `bootstrap/*` harnesses are shell scripts read by
# bash; and `bootstrap/seed/plum.ll` is LLVM IR whose byte-identity is
# asserted by `bootstrap/self-sufficiency`.
#
# Declaring it here rather than relying on each developer's git config
# is the point -- the setting that would corrupt a checkout is one this
# repo cannot see or control.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touch these, whatever they contain.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gz binary
